## Reconciliation / Execution Flow

### Entrypoint (`cmd/virt-v2v/entrypoint.go`)

```
1. Load AppConfig from env/flags
2. Link SSL certificates (vSphere only)
3. Create output directory (/var/tmp/v2v)
4. Branch:

   A. Remote Inspection (IsRemoteInspection=true):
      └─ RunRemoteV2vInspection() → exit

   B. Conversion (IsRemoteInspection=false):
      ├─ In-Place (IsInPlace=true):
      │   ├─ LibvirtUrl set → GetDomainXML() → write /tmp/input.xml
      │   │   └─ OverlayEnabled? RunInPlaceWithOverlay(RunVirtV2vInPlace) : RunVirtV2vInPlace()
      │   └─ No LibvirtUrl → OverlayEnabled? RunInPlaceWithOverlay(RunVirtV2vInPlaceDisk) : RunVirtV2vInPlaceDisk()
      ├─ Cold (default):
      │   └─ RunVirtV2v() → pipes stdout to virt-v2v-monitor
      │
      ├─ RunVirtV2VInspection() → local inspection on converted disks
      ├─ RunCustomize(inspection.OS) → virt-customize
      │   (failure is non-fatal → Warning via server.AddWarning)
      └─ If IsLocalMigration: start HTTP server on :8080
```

### Overlay Flow (`RunInPlaceWithOverlay`)

```
CreateOverlays() → qemu-img create -f qcow2 -b <backing> -F raw <overlay>
  → rewire disk.Link symlinks to overlay
  → run conversion function (writes go to overlay, not base disk)
  → on success: CommitOverlays() → qemu-img commit → restore symlinks
  → on failure: DiscardOverlays() → remove overlays, base disks unchanged
```

### vSphere Input Transport Selection

```
vsphereInputTransport():
  1. VDDK lib dir exists → vddk (-it vddk -io vddk-libdir=... -io vddk-thumbprint=...)
  2. NfcPluginPath exists → nfc (-it nfc -io nfc-thumbprint=...)
  3. Builtin NFC plugin exists → nfc
  4. else → no transport (libvirt only)
```

Remote inspection uses `-io vddk-file=<disk>` or `-io nfc-file=<disk>` depending on transport.

