## Guest Customization (`pkg/virt-v2v/customize/`)

Runs `virt-customize` on converted disks. OS-specific and **non-fatal** (failures produce warnings).

### Windows Scripts (`customize/scripts/windows/`)

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `9999-run-mtv-ps-scripts.bat` | Main firstboot init (standard) |
| `9999-run-mtv-ps-scripts-legacy.bat` | Main firstboot init (legacy VirtIO drivers) |
| `9999-network-config.ps1.tmpl` / `9999-network-config-registry.ps1.tmpl` | Static IP configuration (WMI vs registry) |
| `9999-remove_duplicate_persistent_routes.ps1` / `-registry.ps1` | Clean up duplicate routes |
| `9999-preserve_complementry_ips_per_nic.ps1.tmpl` / `-registry.ps1.tmpl` | Multiple IPs per NIC |
| `9100_cleanup_vmware.ps1` | VMware driver/service cleanup (vSphere only) |
| `verify_vmware_cleanup.ps1` | Post-cleanup verification |
| `5001_win_firstboot_qemu_ga_install.ps1` | QEMU guest agent install |
| `99999-signal-conversion-done.ps1` | Signals CONVERSION_DONE on COM1 (WaitForGuestReboot) |

VMware cleanup scripts are injected when `VsphereVmwareDriverRemoval=true` AND source is vSphere.

### Linux Scripts (`customize/scripts/rhel/`)

- **Run scripts** (`--run`): executed during customization (`network_config_util.sh` handles ifcfg, NetworkManager, netplan, wicked, systemd-networkd)
- **Firstboot scripts** (`--firstboot`): executed on first boot after migration

### Dynamic Scripts

User-supplied scripts at `/mnt/dynamic_scripts`:

- **Windows**: `^([0-9]+_win_firstboot([\w\-]*.ps1))$` → uploaded to Firstboot directory
- **Linux**: `^([0-9]+_linux_(run|firstboot)([\w\-]*.sh))$` → `run` or `firstboot` based on second group

### Static IP Handling

- **Linux**: MAC-to-IP mappings written to `/tmp/macToIP` inside the guest
- **Windows**: Go `text/template` renders PowerShell scripts; supports primary IP, complementary IPs, and DNS. Registry-based variant when `WindowsRegistryNetworkConfig=true`.

### LUKS Encryption

Both virt-v2v and virt-customize accept `--key` args:

- `--key all:clevis` — Clevis/NBDE decryption
- `--key all:file:/etc/luks/<keyfile>` — key files from mounted LUKS directory

